insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1938597d-7ed6-52da-a4b1-5c5960f6a5f5', 'wg6-informative-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-informative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$How Owls Hunt in the Dark$q$, $q$(1) Owls are birds of prey that do most of their hunting at night. (2) Darkness makes finding food hard, yet owls are some of the most successful hunters in the animal world. (3) Their bodies have several special features that help them hunt.

(4) First, owls have very large eyes that collect lots of light. (5) Their eyes are so big that they cannot move them in their sockets. (6) To look around, an owl turns its whole head, and some owls can turn it about three quarters of a full circle.

(7) Owls also have excellent hearing. (8) On many owls, one ear opening sits a little higher than the other. (9) Because of this, a sound reaches each ear at a slightly different time, which helps the owl find exactly where a mouse is hiding. (10) Some owls can even catch prey hidden under snow by using sound alone.

(11) Finally, owls fly almost silently. (12) Their wing feathers have soft, comb-like edges that break up the rush of air. (13) Silent flight is when a bird flies with almost no sound. (14) This lets an owl swoop down before its prey hears it coming.$q$, 'draft')
