-- Passage wg6-informative-writing-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('a72e9f14-01d3-5410-8b44-e2fb77f07bed', 'wg6-informative-writing-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-informative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$How Bicycle Gears Work$q$, $q$(1) Many bicycles have gears that riders can change while they pedal. (2) Gears make it possible to climb steep hills and speed along flat roads on the same bike. (3) To understand how they work, it helps to know the parts involved.

(4) A gear is a wheel with teeth around its edge. (5) On a bike, the chain connects the front gears, near the pedals, to the back gears, on the rear wheel. (6) When the rider pushes the pedals, the chain pulls the back gear and turns the wheel. (7) A lever on the handlebars, called a shifter, moves the chain from one gear to another.

(8) Choosing the right gear depends on the ride. (9) When the chain sits on a small front gear and a large back gear, pedaling feels easy, but the bike moves slowly. (10) This "low gear" is helpful for climbing hills. (11) A large front gear and a small back gear make pedaling harder, but each push sends the bike much farther. (12) This "high gear" works well on flat or downhill roads. (13) My bike is blue and has a basket on the front.$q$, 'draft')
