insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('6feb192d-cc60-5a28-800d-dd58f5b84582', 'wg6-informative-writing-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-informative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Origami: The Art of Paper Folding$q$, $q$(1) Origami is the art of folding a flat sheet of paper into a shape without cutting or gluing it. (2) The word comes from two Japanese words meaning "fold" and "paper." (3) Paper folding has been practiced in Japan for hundreds of years, and today people all over the world enjoy it.

(4) Folders create shapes using a small set of basic folds. (5) A valley fold bends the paper toward you, making a crease shaped like the letter V. (6) A mountain fold bends the paper away from you, so the crease points up like a mountain peak. (7) By combining these folds in different orders, a folder can make animals, flowers, boxes and even stars.

(8) Origami is also useful outside the art room. (9) Engineers have studied folding patterns to design objects that pack flat and open up later. (10) For example, some solar panels for spacecraft are folded tightly for launch and then unfolded in space. (11) Medical researchers have used similar ideas to design tiny tools that unfold inside the body.$q$, 'draft')
