   $q$Which concluding statement best sums up the report?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sweeping is the only skill that really matters in curling.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Curling stones are made of heavy granite.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"With careful aim, quick sweeping and clear calls from the skip, a curling team works together to score.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Many other winter sports are played on snow instead of ice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$With careful aim, quick sweeping and clear calls from the skip, a curling team works together to score.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion pulls together aiming, sweeping and the skip's role, which the report explains. Saying sweeping is the only skill that matters is tempting, but paragraph 3 shows that aim and the skip's calls matter too.$q$, 'draft', '596c78b8-de0a-5cd8-8f7d-56dd06e89c18')
